<p>And as a bonus, Fruit Attraction is also kind of a fashion show (especially female business style 😍). But since we are here for a different purpose, let's talk about technologies.</p>

{{ photo(photos.faJulianaBolanos) }}

<h2><span class="num">1.</span> AI in offices</h2>

<p>The main point is AI in offices: processing warehouse documents, forms, reports, etc. It's built on Generative AI, the strongest AI capability right now. It's great to see service providers filling this niche for fresh produce 🚀</p>

{{ photo(photos.faKacperDach, sizes="(max-width: 520px) 100vw, 420px", class="page-figure--portrait") }}

<h2><span class="num">2.</span> Sensors are everywhere</h2>

<p>Good news: more AI in fields, orchards and greenhouses.</p>
<ul class="post-steps">
  <li><strong>Weather stations:</strong> I lost count, it's already kind of a commodity.</li>
  <li><strong>Irrigation &amp; soil sensors:</strong> often together with weather stations.</li>
  <li><strong>Image sensors:</strong> a few industrial-level cameras (looked pretty like IP65). But most providers in yield forecasting, computer vision &amp; quality control don't invent cameras. They use market hardware &amp; optimise the software.</li>
</ul>

<h2><span class="num">3.</span> Visual AI for quality control</h2>

<p>Since we're on quality control already: several companies offer the same product, visual AI for fresh produce. The scheme is the same; the difference is in price (VC-backed ones ask more), accuracy (hugely depends on how modern your line is), and trust.</p>

<p>So, as usual, please do due diligence before anything serious.</p>

<h2><span class="num">4.</span> Biologicals get their own delivery tech</h2>

<p>Biologicals as part of IPM are getting their own delivery tech. Releasing beneficial insects by drone seems to be 4–6 times more effective than manual release.</p>

<p>Additionally, and warmly welcomed for in-field application: robots on legs and on wheels for phytosanitary treatments and weeding. All of them are worth attention and looked ready for a real field trial :)</p>

{{ photo(photos.faMarcJones) }}

