<h2><span class="num">5.</span> RFID, if you're serious about traceability</h2>

<p>RFID is an interesting direction if you're serious about traceability. Tracking produce from farm to supermarket shelf solves lots of compliance issues. One thing to remember: overlapping. I studied it for a Petiole Pro case study (it's a different story on another day 👍🏼).</p>

<p>Choosing an RFID provider is a responsible decision, like a marriage :) Why? Because once their RFID is in, they have kind of a monopoly for you, and everything next has to align with them.</p>

<p>So choose someone who doesn't just want your money but feels like a team member 🤝</p>

<p>There were also drones for spraying, software of all colours and sizes + lots of smaller physical AI projects for both in-field phenotyping and post harvest.</p>

{{ photo(photos.faRobotArm, sizes="(max-width: 520px) 100vw, 420px", class="page-figure--portrait") }}

